# Event handler pass-through

When the only job of a callback is to invoke a prop with the **same signature** (no extra args, no guard), pass the prop **by reference**.

**Do:**

```tsx
onClick={onClose}
onClick={onBackFromPayment}
```

**Don’t:**

```tsx
onClick={() => onClose()}
onClick={() => onBackFromPayment()}
```

**Allowed exceptions:**

- You inject arguments: `onClick={() => selectItem(id)}`
- You must discard an async result: `onClick={() => void submit()}`
- You combine logic: `onClick={() => { track(); onSave(); }}`
